What does this program print?

```java
class Animal {
    String sound() { return "..."; }
    String speak() { return "I say " + sound(); }
}

class Dog extends Animal {
    @Override
    String sound() { return "woof"; }
}

void main() {
    Animal a = new Dog();
    IO.println(a.speak());
}
```

What does this program print? (It compiles, with a warning about calling a static method through an instance.)

```java
class A {
    static String who() { return "A"; }
    String me() { return "A"; }
}

class B extends A {
    static String who() { return "B"; }
    @Override
    String me() { return "B"; }
}

void main() {
    A x = new B();
    IO.println(x.who() + x.me());
}
```

`Op` is a functional interface with a default method. What does this program print?

```java
interface Op {
    int apply(int x);

    default Op twice() {
        return x -> apply(apply(x));
    }
}

void main() {
    Op inc = x -> x + 3;
    IO.println(inc.twice().twice().apply(1));
}
```
